{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/138757-habits-of-highly-effective-sidereals","id":138757,"title":"Habits of highly effective Sidereals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-15T20:01:02-07:00","id":138757,"title":"Habits of highly effective Sidereals","content":"Since Sidereals have graduated from &quot;sneaky-bastards-who-F*cked-everything-up&quot; to trusted mentors, advisers and friends in 3e, let's talk about using them in the game. The Devs have promised more story opportunities besides teaching Sidereal martial arts, but I'd like to talk about roleplaying interactions. If you have any useful books, websites, or sources of inspiration or philosophy that a Sidereal might teach to teach to Solar (Abyssal, Infernal, Exigent, Dragon Blooded) student.<br /> <br /> Also, if you have any original proverbs, parables or fiction, I'd like to hear that as well.<br /> <br /> We're not looking for &quot;Chicken Soup for the Exalted Soul&quot; or how to be a life coach. We want words of wisdom that will guide heroes on the path to raising up or casting down mighty empires, turning the tide of battle or doing other, nifty heroic things.<br /> <br /> Since I'm starting, here goes:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.bhagavad-gita.org/\" target=\"_blank\">The Bhagavad Gita</a>: The god Krishna encourages a warrior king to accept his destiny. Deeply steeped in spiritualism and philosophy, this is an excellent read.<br /> <a href=\"https://encrypted.google.com/books/about/The_Demon_s_Sermon_on_the_Martial_Arts.html?id=G6xR4hnVbikC\" target=\"_blank\">The Demon's Sermon on the Martial Arts</a>. Required reading for any Dragon-blooded student of swordsmanship. The strong Buddhist bent makes it especially good source material<br /> <br /> And a parable I wrote:<br /> <br /> Once there was a maiden who came to a monastery seeking enlightenment.<br /> After three days, she was granted admittance.<br /> Wordlessly, the abbess ushered her to a small hut in the back, and lit the forge within.<br /> Wordlessly, the abbess took up a hammer and and a leather apron, and began to strike iron ingots, heating them, folding them until they became strong steel.<br /> After the sun had risen and set five times the maiden cried &quot;I came to learn sutras! I came seeking enlightenment! Not pounding iron into steel!&quot;<br /> Looking up from her labors, the abbess put down the hammer.<br /> <br /> &quot;Is there a difference?&quot; she asked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T20:17:29-07:00","id":138788,"title":"","content":"The Art of War, (along with the rest of the seven military classics) is full of short, dense sayings that apply to almost any circumstances. Same with the Dao De Jing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T20:54:48-07:00","id":138837,"title":"","content":"In my last game, my Secrets had a very specific philosophy that she espoused to the Eclipse, whom was the character she used as a point of contact for the group:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://knowyourmeme.com/memes/wheatons-law\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Don't be a dick.&quot;</a><br /> <br /> The implication that, should she decide he was being a dick, he would wake up having died of natural causes (because it's perfectly natural to die when a baneclaw is shoved into your eye and swirled around your brainpan) tended to vary depending on how annoyed she was feeling at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T20:56:01-07:00","id":138851,"title":"","content":"I would suggest the Foundation Series by Asimov. A story about generations of highly competent people working to manipulate the course of humanity's future from the peripheries. Plus you should just look at this for non exalted reasons, it's in my opinion this series of works basically defines the entire genre of science fiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T22:02:25-07:00","id":138942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/138757-habits-of-highly-effective-sidereals?p=138837#post138837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my last game, my Secrets had a very specific philosophy that she espoused to the Eclipse, whom was the character she used as a point of contact for the group:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://knowyourmeme.com/memes/wheatons-law\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Don't be a dick.&quot;</a><br /> <br /> The implication that, should she decide he was being a dick, he would wake up having died of natural causes (because it's perfectly natural to die when a baneclaw is shoved into your eye and swirled around your brainpan) tended to vary depending on how annoyed she was feeling at the moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't it only natural if you happen to be involved in the highschool drama of an always chaotic evil race?f","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T00:03:56-07:00","id":139065,"title":"","content":"I thought they were always trusted mentors...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T00:57:00-07:00","id":139098,"title":"","content":"They're supposed to be... in actual fact, I don't think it's something they're all that good at. I hope they're better at it this edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T01:13:28-07:00","id":139107,"title":"","content":"Sidereals are only difficult to run as trusted advisors when everyone playing already knows what hand hey had in the usurpation. when your players are unaware of this, it's much easier. Additionally, if you want the pc's to trust them, your sidereal npc's need to do things to earn that trust. they should be the obi-wan to an inexperienced circle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T01:37:34-07:00","id":139112,"title":"","content":"I meant more that their powers aren't that useful for being trusted mentors.<br /> There's also the way that after some time they'll lose their Arcane Destiny, and the PCs will start forgetting them.<br /> <br /> It's not that they can't be trusted mentors... I just don't think there's much about them that makes them any better at it than anyone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T01:40:54-07:00","id":139114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NuSoardGraphite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/138757-habits-of-highly-effective-sidereals?p=139065#post139065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought they were always trusted mentors...</div> </div> </div> </div>I read &quot;mentors&quot; as &quot;meteors&quot; and was momentarily delighted at the mental imagery D:","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/46-oramus","name":"Oramus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar46_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T01:49:56-07:00","id":139119,"title":"","content":"I don't have much philosophy, but I do have some tips from experience for someone playing a Sidereal friend of a solaroid circle.<br /> <br /> - Forget what the book says: don't make plans. Elaborate plans <i>never </i>survive contact with the real world, much less contact with the Exalted and even less so contact with the ST. The wise man steers.<br /> <br /> - A little bit of paranoia is not only not crazy but <i>entirely justified</i> in Creation, even more so if you're watching over a Solar circle. Consider at least in passing that every single person your circle meets is out to get the lot of you and how you'd deal with them if so. There's a pretty good chance you'll be right about a fifth of the time, minimum.<br /> <br /> - Communication saves lives. <br /> <br /> - Be polite, be efficient, be thought-provoking. You are trying to teach these people things for the benefit of Creation, and asshole mentors have a real chance of backfire, much more with the kind of <i>princely </i>temperament many Solars have. If you really need to make them pause, momentary confusion and koans work far better.<br /> <br /> - Let them know they're useful. Most Solars enjoy being the ones helping you once or twice - in most cases because they feel they can trust you a bit more if you absolutely need them, and in some cases because the Sun managed to land some actual decent people. Trying to distance yourself too much from them usually only leads to distrust, distrust leads to arguments, and arguments lead to Daiklaves which don't lead to the Dark Side because if you come to that point with a Solar then you're honestly screwed anyway. <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T05:43:04-07:00","id":139215,"title":"","content":"@ NuSoardGraphite &amp; The Wizard of Oz :<br /> <br /> Sidereals are (supposed to be) trusted mentors just like solars are (supposed to be) invincible righteous heroes.<br /> <br /> Story-wise they generally lived up to their respective reputation except the interference of the great curse. Solars (more or less temporally) became evil monsters and sidereals became traitors because of that but's that's it.<br /> <br /> Now they are trusted advisors, in the shadows, of the dragonbloods. I don't think it's an accurate perception to still describe sidereals in the present time as traitors. They &quot;switched sides&quot; but they are generally fully loyal to their new &quot;allegiance&quot;.<br /> <br /> Skillset-wise there are a lot of charms that, if you look carefully at, are very effective at counseling and supporting a leader. A few exemples : <br /> - Anima powers in general<br /> <br /> - for social interactions : Preservation of resolve, Presence in abscence technique, Force Decision, Cash and Murder Games<br /> - for combat : Life Gets Worse Approach, Trouble-Reduction Strategy, Meditation on War, Throne Shadow Style<br /> - for &quot;adventure&quot; : Sky and Rain Mantra, a lot of sail charms, Yellow Path, Blue Vervain Binding<br /> - general cases : Flawless Ceremony (version 2.5), Perfection in Life (2.5), A lot of lore/awareness charms to see the future or predict outcomes of choices, Terminal sanction (as it helps all the team instead fo allowing only he sidereal to interact/kill the spirit)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The fool can only learn from a sage, but only the sage can learn from a fool.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2172-jack-in-the-box","name":"Jack In The Box","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T06:42:12-07:00","id":139255,"title":"","content":"<i>The Once and Future King</i>. In fact, I'd say Merlin makes a great example of a First Age Gold Faction Sidereal. He's willing to put faith in Arthur being a good ruler despite having been witness to a tyrannical, genocidal dictator. The lesson he repeatedly attempts to impart on Arthur is that no matter how righteous your cause, might does <i>not</i> make right.<br /> <br /> Of course, the tricky part is that the setting of Exalted is going to make it almost impossible for a would-be ruler to maintain such lofty ideals.<br /> <br /> This book also notably makes repeated appearances in the X-Men movies, to the point where I had to wonder if the filmmakers were trying to teleport it through viewers' eyes and into their skulls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T07:20:19-07:00","id":139303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agentwestmer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/138757-habits-of-highly-effective-sidereals#post138757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since Sidereals have graduated from &quot;sneaky-bastards-who-F*cked-everything-up&quot; to trusted mentors, advisers and friends in 3e...</div> </div> </div> </div>But this is just so they can stab you in the back or manipulate you to do their will, right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T08:30:03-07:00","id":139344,"title":"","content":"Don't call them Sidereals <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I think it was the Odyssey where the hero uses a thaumaturgical ritual to call up the ghost of an ancient seer to get advice? Maybe that was a Sid wearing a destiny, and he previously arranged for the Solars to get access to the ritual.<br /> <br /> Also, have them usually be scarily accurate but occasionally completely wrong. As a player, too many half-truths would make me paranoid and wonder who this weirdo is, but normal good solid info makes it easy to lead up to an Oops moment. Which makes me think... read some Shadowrun. Specifically, any info about fixers and Mr Johnsons. They have a similar role and similar &quot;will he give me a good deal or will he jump out of a teacup &amp; backstab me?&quot; relationship. The Sidereal is probably as worried about the Solars messing everything up as the Solars worry about getting betrayed by the Sid.<br /> <br /> Knowing the present is much better than guessing the future. Loom, godly contacts, and weird charms can give you reliable info on what the enemy is doing <u>right now</u>. And makes it easier to guess what the Solars will do once they know all this, versus trying to force them to stick to a plan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2678-spoonr","name":"SpoonR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2678_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T08:57:52-07:00","id":139395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack In The Box</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/138757-habits-of-highly-effective-sidereals?p=139215#post139215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@ NuSoardGraphite &amp; The Wizard of Oz :<br /> <br /> Now they are trusted advisors, in the shadows, of the dragonbloods.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think they're all that trusted... they have to use sorcery and blackmail to stop people talking about them. The Empress certainly didn't trust them... of course, she didn't distrust them more than her own children and grandchildren, so she was still willing to work with them.<br /> <br /> Anyway, you are right that there are charms that are useful for them being mentors and advisors and viziers... but I think that, like mist Sidereal charms, they're not as good as they could be. It feels very much to me like the writers went &quot;let's give them a set of wacky powers&quot; some of which coincidentally happen to be related to the roles they're supposed to play, but many aren't (I don't mean this completely, there are some stuff that's thematic, but I feel it could be a lot better in that regard).<br /> <br /> I hope that the 3rd ed charmset is not just an update of the charms they've had for the last 2 sessions, but actually is based around the sort of themes that Sidereals are supposed to be about.<br /> Since the current writers include the guy who wrote Throne Shadow Style (which was, sadly, IMH,O by far the best Sidereal charmset because it was actually all about being a secret master hiding behind your puppets, rather than just some charms which could be used that way by clever players), I am fairly optimistic in that regard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T10:23:14-07:00","id":139483,"title":"","content":"I agree with the spirit of the thread. I like those kind of mentors and Sidereals should be it and they should have nice pithy sayings that suit. <br /> <br /> Generally though, to maybe answer some of the other issues raised here, I think Sidereals tend to be more the sort of viziers who go out and about on the behalf of the monarch on fact finding and problem solving missions and manage the affairs of state, more than advisors who hang around the palace telling the king what to do, training him in a wax on, wax off way and generally inspiring him.<br /> <br /> So they tend to have a lot more magic for being out and about and working out what's going and making events turn out as they like, more than buffing their prince / tool. The Sidereals being the Wise Old Master is where they can be but in general, think more Di Renjie (at least as the Hong Kong film industry has sold him to me...), the masterful official who went out and poked his nose around and so served the Empress, albeit rather more overtly supernatural and sorcerous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T15:50:15-07:00","id":139902,"title":"","content":"On the subject of parables and philosophies the Sidereals might teach to their student... have you read Cult of the Illuminated? Because while it's hardly an original thought of mine, that's the first thing that springs to mind.<br /> <br /> The Prince (in a non-sarcastic way) or similar ancient treatises on politics are very Sidereal as well. It's certainly fitting for a Sidereal to be telling their Solar protege that they need to be brutal, feared, merciless, etc, for the greater good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T23:59:11-07:00","id":140304,"title":"","content":"A Sidereal is...<br /> <br /> ... someone who makes elaborate plans and pulls them off.<br /> ... someone who is trying to guide you to find your true potential.<br /> ... someone who always has a proverb to suit the occasion.<br /> ... someone who is illusive and of whom not much is known.<br /> ... someone who has the most surprising and impressive roster of allies to call on.<br /> ... someone who can assume a myriad of fake identities.<br /> <br /> I guess that means that the ultimate pop culture Sidereal is... wait for it... <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=I0Otmb2yFgw\" data-code=\"I0Otmb2yFgw\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/I0Otmb2yFgw/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div></div> </div> </div>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T14:01:16-07:00","id":140921,"title":"","content":"I think the key detail with this topic is that &quot;wisdom&quot; is highly subjective, and if you compile a list of all pithy parables, koans, and aphorisms, you'll find that a lot of them are in direct opposition to one another. It's more a way of packaging a belief to make it more compelling than a form of especially high-quality belief. And people have an intuitive sense of that, so they tend to distinguish between &quot;profound wisdom&quot; and &quot;bullshit platitudes&quot; on the basis of whether, having heard the thing, they agree with it.<br /> <br /> The kinds of people Sidereals are likely to mentor in an Exalted game tend to be pretty headstrong, and they're not infrequently genius virtuosos who are used to getting their way, so anything that seems packaged as &quot;wisdom&quot; has a risk of putting them off. So the really important thing is to use your Sidereal Cheating Bullshit to ensure that the wisdom you deliver comes at a teachable moment -- give people key help when they're in need, and give them advice that you know for a fact will be highly applicable in the near future, even if you have to secretly arrange it that way. You know how whenever the main character in a TV show gets Words of Wisdom, it becomes relevant later on in the same episode? You want to try to replicate that experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T13:06:59-07:00","id":144770,"title":"","content":"This isn't necessarily &quot;wisdom&quot; per-say, but it is a way that I have introduced Sidereals back into my game. The Age of Sorrows has enough in-fighting between every other faction in creation/Yu Shan that I think it should at least be viable for Celestial Exalts to work together. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">The Scripture of the Healed Mask:</span></b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"><i><span style=\"color:#000000\">There once was a constellation, broken in the heavens</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"><i><span style=\"color:#000000\">An ancient symbol of hidden sins committed between siblings</span></i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"><i><span style=\"color:#000000\">Mercury took the first step and forged a connection between the broken stars</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"><i><span style=\"color:#000000\">After seeing her sister move, Venus instilled peace within all Exalts to prepare them for the coming revelation</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"><i><span style=\"color:#000000\">Mars saw her sisters\u2019 resolve and stopped all battles for a single day so that all might see</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"><i><span style=\"color:#000000\">Jupiter gently placed the forgotten strand back onto the Loom of Fate, revealing the tragic secret that tore the Celestial Exalts apart,</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"><i><span style=\"color:#000000\">and Saturn brought an end to Arcane Fate, tying the final bond that healed the Mask</span></i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"><i><span style=\"color:#000000\">The Chosen of the Stars stood humbled,</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"><i><span style=\"color:#000000\">Gods and Exalts paralyzed by shock.</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"><i><span style=\"color:#000000\">Luna wept, covering all of creation in gentle rain.</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"><i><span style=\"color:#000000\">Solars turned to their Sidereal siblings aware</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"><i><span style=\"color:#000000\">as the Unconquered Sun forgave.</span></i></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1623-asrai","name":"Asrai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1623_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}